# Copy to .env.local (untracked, never committed) — `make run` sources it.
#
# --- Proton Mail (Business plan SMTP submission token) -----------------------
# Generate the token in Proton: Settings → All settings → Mail → IMAP/SMTP →
# SMTP submission. The token is shown once; it is not your account password.
# NEUROSCRIBE_SMTP_USER must be the address the token was issued for, and
# NEUROSCRIBE_MAIL_FROM must use that same address or Proton rejects the mail.
#
# NEUROSCRIBE_SMTP_HOST=smtp.protonmail.ch
# NEUROSCRIBE_SMTP_PORT=465                      # implicit TLS (587 is often blackholed)
# NEUROSCRIBE_SMTP_USER=you@your-domain.com
# NEUROSCRIBE_SMTP_PASS=the-smtp-token
# NEUROSCRIBE_MAIL_FROM='Neuroscribe <you@your-domain.com>'
# NEUROSCRIBE_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8484     # public URL in emailed links
# NEUROSCRIBE_REGISTRATION=open
# NEUROSCRIBE_TRUST_PROXY=1                       # behind a TLS-terminating proxy: trust X-Forwarded-Proto (needed for Secure cookies)
#
# Check it before opening sign-ups:
#   ./neuroscribe mail test you@your-domain.com
#
# --- Local development (mail goes to Mailpit, `make mail-dev`) ---------------
# Inbox at http://localhost:8025 ; nothing leaves the machine.
NEUROSCRIBE_SMTP_HOST=127.0.0.1
NEUROSCRIBE_SMTP_PORT=1025
NEUROSCRIBE_MAIL_FROM='Neuroscribe <noreply@localhost>'
NEUROSCRIBE_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8484
NEUROSCRIBE_REGISTRATION=open
